Package: breakpointdrift
Title: Separate Breakpoint Revisions from Real Change in Antimicrobial Resistance
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Ferrya", email = "114243237+FerrumSL@users.noreply.github.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: When CLSI or EUCAST revises a clinical breakpoint, isolates with the
    same minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) change category, and the share of
    resistant isolates in an antibiogram moves with no change in the bacteria. This
    package reinterprets raw MICs and zone diameters from two periods under both
    guideline editions with the 'AMR' package, splits each organism and drug's change
    in percent resistant into the breakpoint artefact and the real change, tests each
    pair, estimates the shift in the MIC distribution from an interval-censored model
    that uses no breakpoint, and writes a report for a stewardship committee.
